{
  "body0": "New storage capacity gets built at triple redundancy and nobody calls it overreaction. The metric shear condensates presses, Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71 holds, and Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter pays for both: wages frozen until someone blinks. Strip away the filings and the cause is plain — the supply contract renews on terms nobody has seen yet. The principals are Long Hollow Miners Circuit and Mothallah Corridor-631; the casualty ledger, so far, is kept at Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter. The dispute has a second floor: the workers are legally trapped. Cargo that skips inspection moves at night, along routes everyone can name. Freight insurance for the contested run now costs more than the freight. The metric shear condensates wants the right to set tariffs no one else can audit; Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter guards the last berth they can still afford to hold; Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71 gets the freight surcharge that lands on them no matter who wins. The pressure underneath is simple: there is no second source for Mothallah Corridor-631 III Station 71, and everyone has done the math. The ground lease under Mothallah Corridor-631 II Charter predates half the law that governs Mothallah Corridor-631 II.",
